author: codex
estimated_minutes: 20
acceptance_criteria: "A red source-contract regression rejects the stale marker-before-close explanation; The docstring states that markers are removed only after closure succeeds or a closed state is confirmed; The docstring states failed closure preserves both markers for reconciliation; npm run release:check remains exact 100/100/100/100"
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
repro_steps: Read the loadAppliedByTransaction docstring at the exact 58ee095 head and compare its described marker order with compensateCreate.
resolution: "Replace the unsafe pre-fix ordering statement with the actual invariant: compensateCreate removes ownership markers only after closure succeeds or a terminal state was already confirmed, while failed closure retains both markers for reconciliation."
expected_result: "The invariant says marker removal happens only after closure succeeds or the item is confirmed closed, and failed closure retains both markers for reconciliation."
actual_result: The loadAppliedByTransaction docstring now matches compensateCreate and a source-contract regression prevents the stale marker-before-close explanation from returning.
